WEBVTT


00:00:01.550 --> 00:00:02.310
OK.

00:00:02.310 --> 00:00:05.390
Here's a question for you.

00:00:05.390 --> 00:00:08.780
How many of the people
you write for are psychic

00:00:08.780 --> 00:00:10.950
with infallible memories?

00:00:10.950 --> 00:00:12.810
It's a dumb question,
right?

00:00:12.810 --> 00:00:17.450
And yet, it's so,
so easy to treat them as if they are.

00:00:17.450 --> 00:00:19.260
We see it all the time.

00:00:19.260 --> 00:00:21.210
Take this sentence.

00:00:21.210 --> 00:00:23.680
'Owing to the fact that
we have been experiencing

00:00:23.680 --> 00:00:26.270
severe difficulties with our suppliers,

00:00:26.270 --> 00:00:29.610
coupled with industrial action
by postal staff,

00:00:29.610 --> 00:00:35.070
we are sorry to inform you
that your order has been delayed.'

00:00:35.070 --> 00:00:38.870
Let's leave aside the fact
that this is a very long sentence –

00:00:38.870 --> 00:00:41.560
33 words long in fact.

00:00:41.560 --> 00:00:42.190
No.

00:00:42.190 --> 00:00:45.290
We're talking about
the structure here.

00:00:45.290 --> 00:00:49.220
There are two parts
to this sentence.

00:00:49.220 --> 00:00:50.610
What's happening:

00:00:50.610 --> 00:00:53.871
the order has been delayed
and we are sorry.

00:00:53.871 --> 00:00:57.490
And why it's happening:
supplier difficulties,

00:00:57.490 --> 00:00:59.800
industrial action.

00:00:59.800 --> 00:01:03.890
And the writer has put the why first.

00:01:03.890 --> 00:01:06.270
Now, OK,
they may have been thinking

00:01:06.270 --> 00:01:08.200
they'd get their excuses in early,

00:01:08.200 --> 00:01:10.730
but it also does two other things,

00:01:10.730 --> 00:01:13.510
which are bad news for engagement and building

00:01:13.510 --> 00:01:15.150
understanding.

00:01:15.150 --> 00:01:18.730
First,
it keeps the reader guessing.

00:01:18.730 --> 00:01:21.410
They have to read
three-quarters of the sentence

00:01:21.410 --> 00:01:24.540
before they get to the point,
the what.

00:01:24.540 --> 00:01:26.400
When you write
a sentence like that,

00:01:26.400 --> 00:01:29.680
you're asking the reader
to invest their time and energy,

00:01:29.680 --> 00:01:32.350
to set aside whatever
else they're doing,

00:01:32.350 --> 00:01:36.720
and just keep reading,
taking it on trust that it will be worth

00:01:36.720 --> 00:01:37.680
it.

00:01:37.680 --> 00:01:39.760
OK, if you were
building up to telling them

00:01:39.760 --> 00:01:43.314
they'd won the lottery
or even got a job they'd applied for,

00:01:43.314 --> 00:01:44.730
then you can be pretty sure they'd

00:01:44.730 --> 00:01:46.630
be happy to keep reading.

00:01:46.630 --> 00:01:50.160
But for most situations,
you're more likely to just end up

00:01:50.160 --> 00:01:51.860
annoying them.

00:01:51.860 --> 00:01:53.380
And you're also
doing something else

00:01:53.380 --> 00:01:56.710
when you write sentences like this:
you're asking the reader

00:01:56.710 --> 00:02:00.350
to remember that first part
of the sentence, the why,

00:02:00.350 --> 00:02:02.710
while they read the last part.

00:02:02.710 --> 00:02:06.260
And then you're asking them
to recall the first part

00:02:06.260 --> 00:02:08.520
and tack it on to the end.

00:02:08.520 --> 00:02:11.270
That's a lot to ask. Really.

00:02:11.270 --> 00:02:15.090
It's a big drain on
what could be a tired, stressed,

00:02:15.090 --> 00:02:16.850
or busy reader.

00:02:16.850 --> 00:02:20.080
Because, yes, 
hey're just like you.

00:02:20.080 --> 00:02:23.880
Scientists call it cognitive load,
the amount of brain work

00:02:23.880 --> 00:02:26.290
needed to understand something.

00:02:26.290 --> 00:02:28.740
The higher the cognitive load,
the harder

00:02:28.740 --> 00:02:31.190
your reader has to work.

00:02:31.190 --> 00:02:33.710
Wouldn't it be better
to let them save their brainpower

00:02:33.710 --> 00:02:36.930
for retaining what you've said
or thinking about how they'll

00:02:36.930 --> 00:02:38.980
apply the information?

00:02:38.980 --> 00:02:42.920
The main part of a sentence
is what's actually happening.

00:02:42.920 --> 00:02:44.900
Why is secondary.

00:02:44.900 --> 00:02:46.730
Really, it's easy.

00:02:46.730 --> 00:02:50.950
Just write the first part first
and the second part second,

00:02:50.950 --> 00:02:55.430
and you'll make it easy
on the readers and easy on you.

